5},{\"_454\":2264,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2263,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2262,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2261,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2260,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2259,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},\"0wxdp7\",\"t5y2dp\",\"8e5m70\",\"uhcdd3\",\"x74q4e\",\"a7gjuc\",\"p181iq\",\"9ekq20\",\"g42iqu\",\"lf3n6x\",\"ako8k1\",\"7diucm\",\"0djdwu\",{\"_1122\":2282,\"_1124\":-5,\"_1125\":2287,\"_1127\":2288,\"_55\":2289,\"_1130\":2290,\"_40\":-5,\"_1133\":-5,\"_43\":2280,\"_2281\":26},{\"_1122\":2282,\"_1124\":-5,\"_1125\":2283,\"_1127\":2284,\"_55\":2285,\"_1130\":2286,\"_40\":-5,\"_1133\":-5,\"_43\":2280,\"_2281\":26},{\"_1122\":2275,\"_1124\":-5,\"_1125\":2276,\"_1127\":2277,\"_55\":2278,\"_1130\":2279,\"_40\":-5,\"_1133\":-5,\"_43\":2280,\"_2281\":26},\"fileciteturn48file0L2-L2\",5823,5851,[],[],\"hidden\",\"invalid\",\"fileciteturn58file0L2-L2\",4311,4339,[],[],2815,2843,[],[],{\"_2294\":2287,\"_2295\":2288,\"_2296\":2297,\"_2298\":2300},{\"_2294\":2283,\"_2295\":2284,\"_2296\":2297,\"_2298\":2300},{\"_2294\":2276,\"_2295\":2277,\"_2296\":2297,\"_2298\":2299},\"start_ix\",\"end_ix\",\"citation_format_type\",\"berry_file_search\",\"invalid_reason\",\"API tool citation id is not a valid file id: eccd3f0e-65d9-4668-be85-576af261a45e\",\"API tool citation id is not a valid file id: 06e2518e-563a-44de-9529-7ce2d0dff00b\",[1278],[2303],\"Yes — **but with one important correction**:\\n\\n\u003e FOSSIL should not become the place where *literally everything* gets dumped.\\n\\nThat would recreate context rot at the storage layer.\\n\\nWhat you are converging on is closer to an **operating substrate for AI engineering**, where FOSSIL is the durable **knowledge/evidence plane**.\\n\\nA useful decomposition is:\\n\\n```text\\n                 HUMAN\\n                   │\\n          intent / clarification\\n                   │\\n                   ▼\\n             INTENT PLANE\\n     requirements / checkpoints /\\n     invariants / acceptance criteria\\n                   │\\n                   ▼\\n            EXECUTION PLANE\\n      Codex / Claude / Luna / etc.\\n       ephemeral specialized agents\\n                   │\\n          tools through broker\\n                   │\\n                   ▼\\n           VERIFICATION PLANE\\n     tests / fuzz / mutations / TLA+\\n     synthetic users / holdouts /\\n     canaries / benchmarks / critics\\n                   │\\n                   ▼\\n             KNOWLEDGE PLANE\\n                  FOSSIL\\n                   │\\n        durable provenance + state\\n```\\n\\nAnd then a coordination layer watches the whole thing:\\n\\n```text\\nwho did what\\nwhat requirement authorized it\\nwhat implementation changed\\nwhat tests actually ran\\nwhat failed\\nwhat evidence exists\\nwhat remains uncertain\\nwhat decision superseded what\\n```\\n\\nThat's where this becomes much more interesting than “RAG.”\\n\\n## But FOSSIL must distinguish storage classes\\n\\nI would **not** put 10,000 Luna conversations directly into the durable graph.\\n\\nYou might run:\\n\\n```text\\n12,481 synthetic interactions\\n3,200 fuzz cases\\n900 mutations\\n150 critic passes\\n40 model-checking runs\\n```\\n\\nMost of that should live as **operational artifacts**.\\n\\nFOSSIL should retain something closer to:\\n\\n```text\\nEvaluationRun eval_381\\n  generated_cases: 12,481\\n  policy_version: interaction-fuzz-v4\\n  implementation: abc123\\n  requirement_set: reqset_27\\n\\n  PASSED: 12,409\\n  FAILED: 72\\n\\n  failure_clusters:\\n      context-loss-after-correction\\n      wrong-project-isolation\\n      ambiguous-current-state\\n\\n  artifacts:\\n      corpus_hash\\n      raw_run_location\\n      report_hash\\n\\n  minimized_counterexamples:\\n      case_918\\n      case_1261\\n      case_8192\\n```\\n\\nAnd then those minimized failures can become first-class:\\n\\n```text\\nObservation\\n   \\\"current-state answer reverted after compaction\\\"\\n\\nFAILED_BY\\n   interaction-test-918\\n\\nCHALLENGES\\n   claim \\\"context reconstruction preserves corrections\\\"\\n```\\n\\nThat's valuable durable knowledge.\\n\\nThe other 12,478 boring interactions don't need to become graph entities.\\n\\nFOSSIL's research contract already explicitly takes this position: preserve the auditable intellectual/research lineage and compact references, **not every token, hidden chain-of-thought, HTTP trace, or intermediate model message**. fileciteturn58file0L2-L2\\n\\nThat is a crucial anti-pollution invariant.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## The graph then becomes the project's memory of causality\\n\\nNot merely:\\n\\n```text\\nClaim A relates to Claim B\\n```\\n\\nbut:\\n\\n```text\\nHumanRequirement R12\\n        │\\n        ├── MOTIVATED → ResearchRun R9\\n        │\\n        ├── CONSTRAINS → Design D4\\n        │\\n        └── VERIFIED_BY → InteractionSuite I17\\n                               │\\n                               ├── FAILED_BY → Counterexample C81\\n                               │\\n                               └── VERIFIED_BY → Benchmark B29\\n\\nCounterexample C81\\n        │\\n        └── MOTIVATED → Fix F20\\n                              │\\n                              └── IMPLEMENTED_BY → commit abc123\\n                                                        │\\n                                                        └── VERIFIED_BY → I18\\n\\nDecision D5\\n        └── SUPERSEDES → D4\\n```\\n\\nNow six months later an agent can ask:\\n\\n\u003e Why do we preserve old project facts after correction?\\n\\nand FOSSIL can reconstruct:\\n\\n```text\\nhuman explicitly chose historical preservation\\n→ requirement REQ-17\\n→ architecture decision D5\\n→ interaction fuzz found failure C81\\n→ fix abc123\\n→ regression test T97\\n→ current behavior verified by run I18\\n```\\n\\n**That is substantially more useful than ordinary project documentation.**\\n\\nThe research-trace design already aims at exactly this reconstruction of question → alternatives → evidence → decision → implementation → later supersession. fileciteturn58file0L2-L2\\n\\n---\\n\\n# This also solves a major weakness in ephemeral agents\\n\\nIf agents are disposable:\\n\\n```text\\nAgent A dies.\\nAgent B starts fresh.\\nAgent C comes next week.\\n```\\n\\nthey can't depend on:\\n\\n\u003e “Remember what Agent A figured out.”\\n\\nInstead:\\n\\n```text\\nagent state = disposable\\nproject state = durable\\n```\\n\\nAgent B asks FOSSIL:\\n\\n```text\\nWhat is current?\\nWhat is provisional?\\nWhat failed?\\nWhat was tried?\\nWhat requirements constrain this?\\nWhat decisions are superseded?\\nWhat unresolved assumptions remain?\\nWhat tests must not regress?\\n```\\n\\nThen receives a bounded context packet.\\n\\nThis is precisely how you reduce context rot without requiring immortal agent conversations.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# And provenance becomes much richer than Git history\\n\\nGit answers:\\n\\n\u003e **What code changed?**\\n\\nIt doesn't reliably answer:\\n\\n\u003e Why was this chosen?\\n\\n\u003e Which human requirement required it?\\n\\n\u003e Which alternative lost?\\n\\n\u003e What benchmark disproved the original assumption?\\n\\n\u003e Which user simulation found the bug?\\n\\n\u003e Was the decision provisional at the time?\\n\\n\u003e Was the test written before or after the implementation?\\n\\n\u003e Which agent generated the candidate?\\n\\n\u003e Did the same agent generate the oracle?\\n\\n\u003e Which model/runtime/version produced the research?\\n\\nThose are FOSSIL questions.\\n\\nThe existing event format already supports separate actor identity, model/harness/skill versions, causal event IDs, evidence references, source snapshots, software commit, ontology/retrieval-policy versions and benchmark references. fileciteturn48file0L2-L2\\n\\nSo there's already a foundation for that provenance graph.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# I would be careful with the phrase “OS”\\n\\nBut it's actually useful if we define it correctly.\\n\\nNot:\\n\\n\u003e FOSSIL becomes one gigantic AI operating system.\\n\\nThat would be catastrophic scope explosion.\\n\\nInstead:\\n\\n```text\\nAI Engineering OS\\n│\\n├── Intent subsystem\\n│     requirements elicitation\\n│\\n├── Work scheduler / task broker\\n│\\n├── Agent runtimes\\n│     Codex / Claude / Luna / others\\n│\\n├── Tool broker\\n│     Git / CI / TLA+ / fuzzers / browsers\\n│\\n├── Verification subsystem\\n│\\n├── Human interaction subsystem\\n│\\n└── Durable knowledge/evidence subsystem\\n      FOSSIL\\n```\\n\\n**FOSSIL owns the last one.**\\n\\nMaybe also stable contracts for supplying context to the others.\\n\\nBut it should not become the agent scheduler, TLA+ runner, IDE, model router, CI system and human-interface system.\\n\\nThat's how we prevent the “OS” idea from swallowing the project.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## And there is a beautiful recursive property here\\n\\nThe system can use itself to remember **how the AI engineering system itself evolved**.\\n\\nFor example:\\n\\n```text\\nRequirement:\\n\\\"Human attention is expensive.\\\"\\n\\nResearch:\\ninteractive clarification papers\\n\\nDecision:\\nIntent Agent before implementation\\n\\nPrototype:\\nintent-agent-v1\\n\\nEvaluation:\\n78 ambiguous tasks\\n\\nObservation:\\nasked 41% unnecessary questions\\n\\nDecision:\\nintroduce question-value scoring\\n\\nPrototype:\\nintent-agent-v2\\n\\nEvaluation:\\nsame holdout set\\n\\nResult:\\nhuman turns ↓\\nrequirement misses ↓\\n\\nPromotion:\\nv2 becomes default\\n```\\n\\nFOSSIL records the entire lineage.\\n\\nSo five generations later, nobody has to say:\\n\\n\u003e “Why on earth is this weird question-ranking mechanism here?”\\n\\nThe reason is queryable.\\n\\n---\\n\\n# I think the combined idea is becoming:\\n\\n**Agents are processes.**  \\nThey can be ephemeral and replaceable.\\n\\n**Tools are capabilities.**  \\nThey should be brokered and constrained.\\n\\n**Requirements are durable human-authoritative state.**\\n\\n**Tests/benchmarks/fuzz/model checking are evidence generators.**\\n\\n**Models generate candidates and counterexamples, not truth.**\\n\\n**FOSSIL preserves the durable causal/evidentiary history connecting all of them.**\\n\\nAnd:\\n\\n\u003e **The human's scarce attention should be spent resolving semantic uncertainty, while cheap inference and compute do almost everything possible before and after that interaction.**\\n\\nThat is much closer to a coherent “AI work OS” than trying to make one super-agent smart enough to remember, plan, code, test, critique, judge itself, and somehow infer what the human meant.\",{},{\"_454\":2229,\"_461\":2308,\"_47\":2309,\"_465\":2310,\"_467\":468,\"_469\":14,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":2311,\"_474\":475},\"bbb214d5-df2a-4a28-a00a-0053dd7f60c1\",[2213],{\"_1284\":1285,\"_472\":2317},1786907519.441077,{\"_1279\":1305,\"_465\":2316},{\"_1296\":1297,\"_1298\":941,\"_1299\":2312,\"_1301\":2313,\"_1303\":2314,\"_493\":494,\"_495\":2242,\"_497\":498,\"_499\":2243,\"_501\":2243,\"_490\":60,\"_502\":60,\"_59\":60,\"_503\":504,\"_505\":14,\"_506\":2315,\"_507\":2244,\"_509\":26,\"_510\":2245,\"_512\":10},1786907514.3068614,1786907519.3874485,\"hide_all\",\"a5125670-113b-4d1b-a522-4e1667bf1178\",\"Worked for 5s\",{},{\"_454\":2306,\"_461\":2321,\"_47\":2322,\"_49\":2323,\"_465\":2324,\"_467\":468,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":2325,\"_474\":475},\"a188a576-d2ab-4a3d-88ff-623a85e0ea06\",[2229],{\"_1284\":1539,\"_472\":2333},1786907512.302171,1786907548.623904,{\"_1279\":1280,\"_1281\":2331},{\"_502\":60,\"_59\":60,\"_1422\":14,\"_483\":2326,\"_1482\":2327,\"_1525\":2328,\"_1527\":14,\"_1528\":2329,\"_1530\":14,\"_1531\":14,\"_1532\":14,\"_1533\":14,\"_1534\":2330,\"_510\":2245,\"_507\":2244,\"_495\":2242,\"_1536\":-5,\"_499\":2243,\"_501\":2243,\"_490\":60,\"_512\":10,\"_505\":14},[],[],[],[],{},[2332],\"Oh yeah two even more importanr rhinfs i missed are knowledge graoh, everything generated and done should be saved there for provenence as well \\n\\nYrsh absically trhing build an os for ai work \\n\\nThsts where fossil comes in\",{},{\"_454\":2319,\"_461\":2337,\"_47\":2338,\"_49\":2339,\"_465\":2340,\"_467\":468,\"_469\":26,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":2341,\"_474\":475,\"_476\":477},\"ffff6383-0d6e-4272-b625-28dc90692568\",[2306],{\"_1284\":1285,\"_472\":2842},1786906896.434517,1786906951.668459,{\"_1279\":1280,\"_1281\":2840},{\"_478\":2342,\"_480\":26,\"_481\":2343,\"_483\":2344,\"_55\":2345,\"_2346\":2347,\"_486\":2348,\"_488\":2349,\"_490\":60,\"_491\":2350,\"_493\":494,\"_495\":2351,\"_497\":498,\"_499\":2352,\"_501\":2352,\"_502\":60,\"_59\":60,\"_503\":504,\"_505\":26,\"_506\":2335,\"_507\":2353,\"_509\":26,\"_510\":2354,\"_512\":10},{\"_43\":1275,\"_1276\":2839},[2524,2525,2526,2527,2528,2529,2530,2531,2532,2533,2534,2535,2536,2537,2538,2539,2540,2541,2542,2543],[2408,2409],[2395,2396,1590,2397,2398,2399,2400,2401,2402,2403,2404,1594,1595,2405,1598,1599,1600,2406,2407],\"view_state\",{\"_2379\":2380},[],[],{\"_513\":2355,\"_515\":2356,\"_517\":2357,\"_519\":2358,\"_521\":2359,\"_523\":2360,\"_525\":2361,\"_527\":2362,\"_529\":2363,\"_531\":2364,\"_533\":2365,\"_535\":2366},\"wfr_01a00bef9bef73ed96b7d28014ca1d35\",\"d1c43515-a4d4-411d-b9c4-c46cd59cd5a9\",\"saserver-centralus-prod.fck9d:conversation-turn-d1c43515-a4d4-411d-b9c4-c46cd59cd5a9:US\",\"conversation-turn-d1c43515-a4d4-411d-b9c4-c46cd59cd5a9\",{\"_454\":2378,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2377,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2376,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2375,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2374,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2373,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2372,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2371,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2370,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2369,\"_580\":14,\"_581\":14,\"_582\":-5},{\"_454\":2368,\"_580\":14,\"_5