n id is not a valid file id: 28e68f66-1ba7-4ecb-b15f-da9b32cad701\",\"API tool citation id is not a valid file id: 4de8f9a4-d22a-43e4-a996-848b667ff034\",\"API tool citation id is not a valid file id: 18fba48d-5af5-4a4b-9844-6e742ebd8949\",[1278],[9515],\"Yes — **we still need one concrete, fully working FOSSIL RAG build**. “Replaceable” means we can swap components later; it does **not** mean FOSSIL should exist only as schemas and rebuild proofs.\\n\\nHere’s how the pieces are supposed to fit.\\n\\n**Packs are the knowledge boundaries.** A project pack contains project-specific knowledge and can mount shared/domain packs read-only. For example, the plugin-harness project pack can read the shared/common pack but can only write back to its own project pack; moving knowledge upward into a domain/common pack is an explicit promotion rather than an agent casually editing shared knowledge. fileciteturn44file0L2-L2 FOSSIL enforces those read/write mounts in `PackAccess`. fileciteturn33file0L2-L2\\n\\n**Graphiti + Neo4j is the current concrete graph build.** Accepted FOSSIL events are projected into Graphiti, and each stable `pack_id` becomes the Graphiti `group_id`, so project/domain/common knowledge stays separated while relationships and history can still be traversed. fileciteturn40file0L2-L2 This has already been proven against a real Graphiti + Neo4j instance, not just mocks. fileciteturn47file0L2-L2\\n\\nThen there is the actual **RAG layer**. Durable pack events are replayed into retrieval documents containing claims, relations, lifecycle state, evidence references, citations, etc. fileciteturn43file0L2-L2 The currently accepted baseline is:\\n\\n**local BGE embeddings → retrieval → lifecycle/lineage checks → BudgetedContextProvider → agent context**, with BM25 as the degraded fallback. The pinned primary is `BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5`; LiteLLM is **not required** for this baseline. fileciteturn46file0L2-L2\\n\\nAnd this is the important part: **the pieces exist, but the final agent-facing integration is incomplete.** FOSSIL already has an MCP-shaped agent interface exposing `search`, `read`, `lineage`, `propose`, `validate`, `commit`, etc., but its current `CorpusService.search()` is still basically scanning durable events for matching text rather than routing through the richer BGE/Graphiti/context pipeline. fileciteturn32file0L2-L2\\n\\nSo the thing we eventually need is roughly:\\n\\n```text\\nCodex / Claude / OpenCode / Cortex V5\\n                 |\\n              MCP/API\\n                 |\\n        FOSSIL ContextProvider\\n          /      |       \\\\\\n       BGE     BM25     lineage\\n         \\\\        |       /\\n            Graph/claims\\n          Graphiti + Neo4j\\n                 |\\n       project/domain/common packs\\n                 |\\n        durable events/evidence\\n                 |\\n          local FS / R2\\n```\\n\\nAnd **yes, preflight/closeout is one of the main reasons for this**. The engineering-preflight system explicitly says FOSSIL retrieval should supply task-relevant architecture/engineering evidence alongside a live GitHub read. The validator itself remains offline so an outage doesn't prevent work, but when FOSSIL is available it gives the agent the correct project history, current decisions, known failures, architecture rules, etc. fileciteturn41file0L2-L2 fileciteturn42file0L2-L2\\n\\nSo for example:\\n\\n**Before Codex works:**  \\n“I'm modifying storage” → FOSSIL mounts `common engineering + domain storage + project fossil-core` → retrieves relevant decisions/incidents/contracts → generates preflight context.\\n\\n**While V5 works:**  \\nV5 asks FOSSIL for relevant context/lineage instead of dumping the whole corpus into the model.\\n\\n**After the agent finishes:**  \\ntests + outcome + discovered lesson → closeout receipt → useful new knowledge is proposed into the **project pack**; later, genuinely reusable lessons can be promoted into a **domain/common pack**.\\n\\nSo I think you were right to flag this: **after the R2 durability proof, the highest-value FOSSIL work is probably making this single end-to-end local RAG runtime real and easy to use**, rather than doing more abstract infrastructure work. That can start local on your PC with **Graphiti/Neo4j + local BGE + FOSSIL MCP/API**, and Cortex V5/LiteLLM do not need to be modified while we build it.\",{},{\"_454\":9424,\"_461\":9520,\"_47\":9521,\"_465\":9522,\"_467\":468,\"_469\":14,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":9523,\"_474\":475},\"1f0e14f1-0e9a-4531-a5cb-662a527d836f\",[9408],{\"_1284\":1285,\"_472\":9528},1786904245.588821,{\"_1279\":1305,\"_465\":9527},{\"_1296\":1297,\"_1298\":9524,\"_1299\":9525,\"_1301\":9526,\"_1303\":1304,\"_493\":494,\"_495\":9437,\"_497\":498,\"_499\":9438,\"_501\":9438,\"_490\":60,\"_502\":60,\"_59\":60,\"_503\":504,\"_505\":14,\"_506\":9518,\"_507\":9439,\"_509\":26,\"_510\":9440,\"_512\":10},64,1786904181.3988073,1786904245.5667126,\"Worked for 1m 4s\",{},{\"_454\":9518,\"_461\":9532,\"_47\":9533,\"_465\":9534,\"_467\":468,\"_469\":14,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":9535,\"_474\":475},\"2fb2ab26-49da-4c4b-9349-bd0256fb7eca\",[9424],{\"_1284\":1285,\"_472\":9545},1786904245.575454,{\"_1279\":1376,\"_1376\":9540,\"_1378\":9541},{\"_1315\":9536,\"_1296\":1317,\"_1318\":8977,\"_1320\":9537,\"_1322\":1323,\"_1299\":9525,\"_493\":494,\"_1324\":1325,\"_495\":9437,\"_497\":498,\"_499\":9438,\"_501\":9438,\"_490\":60,\"_502\":60,\"_59\":60,\"_503\":504,\"_505\":14,\"_506\":9530,\"_507\":9439,\"_509\":26,\"_510\":9440,\"_512\":10},{\"_1332\":9538},[8979],[9539],\"9820033b-92ad-4514-83b6-1aaffc70c65d\",[9542],\"82ad955a-d2de-40b0-9855-d45d0e00c9d5\",{\"_1381\":9543,\"_465\":1132,\"_1383\":9544,\"_1385\":26},\"Designed a unified FOSSIL retrieval stack and explained Graphiti Neo4j context packs\",[],{},{\"_454\":9530,\"_461\":9549,\"_47\":9550,\"_465\":9551,\"_467\":468,\"_469\":14,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":9552,\"_474\":475},\"a49e57b0-bf04-47c8-907