anly. fileciteturn22file0L2-L2 Current `main` contains both `src/fossil_core` and the old `dkg` compatibility shim. fileciteturn24file0L2-L2\\n\\nSo I’d describe the current state as:\\n\\n**FOSSIL is packaged, but not fully “productized” yet.** It is currently version `0.1.0`, installable as `fossil-core`, and exposes a Python API, but it does **not yet look like a polished local application/daemon/CLI with one-command setup**. fileciteturn26file0L2-L2 The public Python API currently exposes things like `ArtifactStore`, `DurableEventStore`, lifecycle and pack interfaces rather than a finished `FossilClient` experience. fileciteturn28file0L2-L2\\n\\nI think the sensible FOSSIL path now is:\\n\\n**finish R2 durability → make the local-PC FOSSIL experience boring/easy → finish productization/API/CLI.**\\n\\nThat would give you something you can install on your PC, work with locally, and optionally sync its durable truth to R2 — **without needing Cortex V5 or LiteLLM at all.**\",{},{\"_454\":9927,\"_461\":10003,\"_47\":10004,\"_465\":10005,\"_467\":468,\"_469\":14,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":10006,\"_474\":475},\"d01793c8-d002-45eb-9db0-c107d4a360b0\",[9907],{\"_1284\":1285,\"_472\":10009},1786904023.744002,{\"_1279\":1305,\"_465\":2853},{\"_1296\":1297,\"_1298\":2850,\"_1299\":10007,\"_1301\":10008,\"_1303\":1304,\"_493\":494,\"_495\":9939,\"_497\":498,\"_499\":9940,\"_501\":9940,\"_490\":60,\"_502\":60,\"_59\":60,\"_503\":504,\"_505\":14,\"_506\":10001,\"_507\":9941,\"_509\":26,\"_510\":9942,\"_512\":10},1786903962.6421816,1786904023.7354722,{},{\"_454\":10001,\"_461\":10013,\"_47\":10014,\"_465\":10015,\"_467\":468,\"_469\":14,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":10016,\"_474\":475},\"0196b178-1d4e-4c53-99ef-b0c99b7700c2\",[9927],{\"_1284\":1285,\"_472\":10026},1786904023.740105,{\"_1279\":1376,\"_1376\":10021,\"_1378\":10022},{\"_1315\":10017,\"_1296\":1317,\"_1318\":8977,\"_1320\":10018,\"_1322\":1323,\"_1299\":10007,\"_493\":494,\"_1324\":1325,\"_495\":9939,\"_497\":498,\"_499\":9940,\"_501\":9940,\"_490\":60,\"_502\":60,\"_59\":60,\"_503\":504,\"_505\":14,\"_506\":10011,\"_507\":9941,\"_509\":26,\"_510\":9942,\"_512\":10},{\"_1332\":10019},[8979],[10020],\"a5f60b2c-5008-41a4-ac30-dd904a9123f5\",[10023],\"39af4401-a887-4493-bea5-ddd4b485aaad\",{\"_1381\":10024,\"_465\":1132,\"_1383\":10025,\"_1385\":26},\"Reviewed Fossil Core Issue #79 and closure context\",[],{},{\"_454\":10011,\"_461\":10030,\"_47\":10031,\"_465\":10032,\"_467\":468,\"_469\":14,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":10033,\"_474\":475},\"01bd63bc-2e35-4fac-8541-c9da5948eaed\",[10001],{\"_1284\":1285,\"_472\":10046},1786904022.508984,{\"_1279\":1376,\"_1376\":10038,\"_1378\":10037},{\"_1296\":1317,\"_1320\":10034,\"_488\":10035,\"_481\":10036,\"_490\":60,\"_1397\":26,\"_1398\":26,\"_1399\":471,\"_493\":494,\"_495\":9939,\"_497\":498,\"_499\":9940,\"_501\":9940,\"_502\":60,\"_59\":60,\"_503\":504,\"_506\":10037,\"_1401\":1402,\"_1322\":1323,\"_1299\":10007,\"_1324\":1325,\"_505\":14,\"_507\":9941,\"_509\":26,\"_510\":9942,\"_512\":10},[8979],[],[],\"a10714ef-7540-4362-9606-25607ea7744b\",[10039,10040],{\"_1381\":10043,\"_465\":10044,\"_1383\":10045,\"_1385\":26},{\"_1381\":10041,\"_465\":1132,\"_1383\":10042,\"_1385\":26},\"Assessed project status\",[],\"Assessing project status\",\"I’m distinguishing three pieces: what’s already packaged, what the retrieval workflow needs, and what remains experimental. The repository is installable, but it isn’t yet a polished end-user application.\\n\\n**LiteLLM’s role**\\n\\nI’m treating LiteLLM embeddings and reranking as optional hosted-model candidates for the retrieval benchmark—not requirements for the core package. Local sentence-transformer embeddings can support the semantic path instead. fileciteturn0file1\\n\\n**Current productization**\\n\\nI’m seeing a real installable package, `fossil_core`, with tests and recent packaging work merged. However, the public surface still centers on lower-level stores and utilities rather than a streamlined client application. fileciteturn0file0 fileciteturn0file1\\n\\n**Local usability**\\n\\nI’m concluding that cloning and installing it on a PC is practical now, especially for development and experiments. A polished CLI, hosted service, or production-ready workflow still appears to be future work.\",[],{},{\"_454\":10028,\"_461\":10050,\"_47\":10051,\"_49\":10052,\"_465\":10053,\"_467\":468,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":10054,\"_474\":475,\"_476\":1507},\"5d3bcbc5-ec67-4fea-ba1c-510a7a608de1\",[10011],{\"_1284\":1451,\"_1452\":9039,\"_472\":10058},1786904014.6700578,1786904039.605844,{\"_1279\":1280,\"_1281\":10057},{\"_1446\":10055,\"_1299\":10007,\"_493\":494,\"_499\":9940,\"_501\":9940,\"_506\":10056,\"_512\":10,\"_1448\":26},\"Reviewing Issue Comments for Closure Context\",\"f884da93-1d6f-4835-8659-ea430ab469c6\",[1450],{},{\"_454\":10048,\"_461\":10062,\"_47\":10063,\"_49\":10064,\"_465\":10065,\"_467\":468,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":10066,\"_474\":475,\"_476\":1507},\"c2deb723-ea41-4d02-86c9-420bcc066f9d\",[10028],{\"_1284\":1451,\"_1452\":9039,\"_472\":10070},1786904010.199522,1786904039.652082,{\"_1279\":1280,\"_1281\":10069},{\"_1446\":10067,\"_1299\":10007,\"_493\":494,\"_499\":9940,\"_501\":9940,\"_506\":10068,\"_512\":10,\"_1448\":26},\"Fetching Fossil Core Issue #79\",\"26611d19-3aba-4280-8de0-f23da8982da8\",[1450],{},{\"_454\":10060,\"_461\":10074,\"_47\":10075,\"_49\":10076,\"_465\":10077,\"_467\":468,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":10078,\"_474\":475,\"_476\":1507},\"f6807230-800c-42ed-8b84-96cc0b07b412\",[10048],{\"_1284\":1451,\"_1452\":9039,\"_472\":10082},1786904006.1691191,1786904039.097526,{\"_1279\":1280,\"_1281\":10081},{\"_1446\":10079,\"_1299\":10007,\"_493\":494,\"_499\":9940,\"_501\":9940,\"_506\":10080,\"_512\":10,\"_1448\":26},\"Reviewing public API initialization\",\"3c11567b-625d-4309-8326-4f6af6cb7c90\",[1450],{},{\"_454\":10072,\"_461\":10085,\"_47\":10086,\"_49\":10087,\"_465\":10088,\"_467\":468,\"_470\":471,\"_472\":10089,\"_474\":475